units.what:
A dry supervisor job `nhs-ods-census`. It walks organization_mentions in rowid windows, keeping rows whose raw_identifier normalises to a `GBNHS` prefix or whose scheme is 'GB-NHS'. It uses the injected `nhs_ods_org_code` and `org_name_norm`, the same ruler prevention will use.

Its stored report `nhs-ods-census` holds:
- per tail: count, distinct orgs, decision (exact, fold or refused), country spread (GB / NULL / other), first and last notice date;
- per (identity, name_norm): every holder org, uncapped (fixing the 5-holder cap that hid 35 of 304 holders in 11 codes), whether the org is provisional or carries an identifier, mention count, and the posted name verdict if any;
- per code: coded share of SAME bodies by notice year;
- country-less GB-NHS mentions; bare 3-letter values under scheme GB-NHS (out of reach); standing org rows already carrying a GBNHS digit-rule-family identity;
- a gate summary for G1–G5.

A heavy scan belongs in a job, not /v1/sql.

